    <section id="what-is-a-cheap-e-invoicing-solution-in">
      <h2>What is a cheap e-invoicing solution in Dubai?</h2>
<p>A cheap e-invoicing solution is an accredited service provider (ASP) route with the lowest total cost over three years. It is not the lowest sticker price. It counts setup, yearly fees, per-invoice fees and your own time. The cheapest route is usually accounting software that is itself an ASP, such as Wafeq, TallyPrime or Zoho Books.</p>
<p>That is the short version. The rest of this guide shows the real numbers.</p>
<p>Why does this matter now? Because every UAE business that sells to other businesses must send e-invoices. If your revenue is under AED 50 million, you must appoint an ASP by <b>31 March 2027</b> and go live on <b>1 July 2027</b>. Miss the first date and the fine is AED 5,000 for each month.</p>
<p>So you need a provider. The question is how to avoid paying more than you must.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="5-cheap-e-invoicing-solutions-in-dubai-c">
      <h2>5 cheap e-invoicing solutions in Dubai, compared</h2>
<p>Here are the five cheapest routes, ranked by three-year cost at about 500 invoices a year. All prices are in AED and exclude 5% VAT.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="w700"><thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Solution</th><th>Is it an ASP?</th><th>What you pay (about 500 invoices)</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>1</td><td class="txt">Wafeq</td><td class="txt">Yes</td><td class="txt">Plan from 690 a year. E-invoicing included</td><td class="txt">Small firms that want accounting and e-invoicing together</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td class="txt">TallyPrime</td><td class="txt">Yes</td><td class="txt">Active TSS, about 468 a year (Silver). No per-invoice fee</td><td class="txt">Traders and distributors with many invoices</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td class="txt">Zoho Books</td><td class="txt">Yes</td><td class="txt">Professional plan at 90 a month, plus packs (500 = 185)</td><td class="txt">Service firms that want cloud accounting</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td class="txt">Excel / no software</td><td class="txt">No (we add one)</td><td class="txt">4,000 first year, then 1,500</td><td class="txt">Businesses with a few hundred invoices a year</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td class="txt">QuickBooks Online or Desktop</td><td class="txt">No (we add one)</td><td class="txt">6,000 or 7,000 first year, then 1,500</td><td class="txt">Businesses that want to keep QuickBooks</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Using Odoo, Sage, Xero, SAP or another ERP? Your route costs about the same as the Excel route, 4,000 plus a connector in year one. Then it is 1,500 a year. The connector is quoted by message, because each system connects differently.</p>
<p>Notice the gap. The first three solutions cost between AED 690 and about AED 1,300 a year. The last two cost more in year one, because you pay for registration, setup and sometimes a connector.</p>
<p>That does not make them bad. If you love your software, keeping it can still be the smart choice. We cover that in Way 6. The seven ways below show you how to pick between all five.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-1-check-if-your-software-is-already">
      <h2>Way 1: Check if your software is already an ASP</h2>
<p>This is the biggest money saver. Start here.</p>
<p>An ASP is a provider approved by the UAE Ministry of Finance. It checks each invoice, converts it to the UAE format (called PINT AE), sends it over the Peppol network and reports the data to the Federal Tax Authority (FTA).</p>
<p>Three accounting programs are ASPs themselves:</p>
<ul class="know"><li><b>Zoho Books.</b> Zoho Software Trading LLC is on the Ministry of Finance list.</li><li><b>TallyPrime.</b> Tally Software Solutions FZCO is on the list.</li><li><b>Wafeq.</b> Wafeq FZ-LLC is on the list.</li></ul>
<p>If you use one of these, you appoint your software company on EmaraTax. That is the FTA portal. You do not hire a second provider. You do not pay a connector fee. You do not run two systems.</p>
<p>If you use QuickBooks, Excel, Odoo, Sage, Xero or SAP, the story is different. These tools are not ASPs. You need an outside ASP and a way to connect it. That adds cost.</p>
<p>Here is a simple example. Maya runs a small cleaning company in Dubai. She uses Wafeq Starter at AED 690 a year. Her e-invoicing cost is AED 0 on top of that. Now picture her neighbour, Ravi, who uses QuickBooks Online. Ravi pays AED 6,000 in year one for the same job. The gap is not about quality. It is about where the ASP sits.</p>
<p>Not sure if your software is an ASP? Check the Ministry of Finance list. Or message us. We tell you in minutes.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-2-count-your-invoices-before-you-com">
      <h2>Way 2: Count your invoices before you compare prices</h2>
<p>Every price you see depends on one number. How many invoices do you send in a year?</p>
<p>Count these:</p>
<ul class="know"><li>Sales invoices you send to businesses and government.</li><li>Credit notes you send.</li></ul>
<p>Do not count these:</p>
<ul class="know"><li>Invoices you receive from suppliers. (With us, they are free. Some providers count them, so ask.)</li><li>Sales to consumers (B2C). They are outside e-invoicing for now.</li></ul>
<p>Here are two quick ways to count. Look at last year's invoice numbers. Subtract the first number from the last. Or take one busy month and multiply by 12.</p>
<p>Then add 10% to 20% if you plan to grow.</p>
<p>Why does the count matter so much? Because prices work in different ways. Wafeq and Tally charge no per-invoice fee. Zoho sells packs. Outside ASPs charge a fixed amount for a set number of invoices. A business with 120 invoices a year and a business with 5,000 should not pick the same plan.</p>
<p>Small volume changes the answer. Say you send 300 invoices a year. Zoho packs cost about AED 111. With a Professional plan at AED 1,080, you spend AED 1,191 in year one. Our Excel route costs AED 4,000 in year one for the same 300 invoices. At 5,000 invoices, Zoho costs about AED 2,580 in year one. The Excel route costs AED 7,375.</p>
<p>Know your number first. Then compare.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-3-confirm-accreditation-and-real-pin">
      <h2>Way 3: Confirm accreditation and real PINT AE support</h2>
<p>Cheap is risky if the provider is not accredited.</p>
<p>Only providers on the Ministry of Finance list can legally send your invoices and report the tax data. The list has more than 80 providers. It changes often, so check it on the day you sign.</p>
<p>Look for the provider's <b>legal company name</b> on the list. Some sellers are resellers. They sell an accredited provider's service under their own brand. That is fine, but ask who the accredited provider is. If nobody can tell you, walk away.</p>
<p>Also check the format. A PDF is not an e-invoice in the UAE. An e-invoice is structured data in the PINT AE format. Your customer's system reads it. Nobody retypes anything. If a tool only makes a nice-looking PDF, it will not meet the rule.</p>
<p>Ask these two questions before you pay:</p>
<ol class="know"><li>"Which accredited provider will send my invoices?"</li><li>"Do you create PINT AE files, or only PDFs?"</li></ol>
<p>A good provider answers both in one line. A weak one changes the subject.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-4-compare-year-one-year-two-and-year">
      <h2>Way 4: Compare year one, year two and year three</h2>
<p>Many buyers compare only the first-year price. That hides the real cost.</p>
<p>Outside-ASP routes have big one-time fees. Built-in routes have small yearly fees. If you look only at year one, you miss how the costs behave over time.</p>
<p>Here is the formula we use for software that needs an outside ASP. The letter n is the number of invoices and credit notes you send in a year.</p>
<pre style="overflow-x:auto;background:#f4f6fa;padding:14px;border-radius:8px;font-size:.85rem">Invoice fee       = 500                      if n is 500 or less
                  = 500 + 0.75 × (n − 500)   if n is more than 500

One-time fees     = Onboarding 1,000 + Setup 1,500 + Connector
Connector         = QuickBooks Online 2,000
                    QuickBooks Desktop 3,000
                    Excel 0
                    Other software: quoted on WhatsApp

First year        = One-time fees + Platform fee 1,000 + Invoice fee
Every year after  = Platform fee 1,000 + Invoice fee</pre>
<p>There are no slabs or brackets. Above 500 invoices, you pay for your exact count. So your average price per invoice keeps falling. It is AED 1.00 at 500 invoices, about AED 0.88 at 1,000 and about AED 0.76 at 10,000.</p>
<p>Now look at three years. This table uses 500 invoices a year. It shows e-invoicing costs only. Your accounting software subscription is separate, except for Wafeq, where the plan is your accounting software.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="w700"><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Year 1</th><th>Year 2</th><th>Year 3</th><th>Three-year total</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="txt">Wafeq Starter</td><td>690</td><td>690</td><td>690</td><td>2,070</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">TallyPrime Silver (new licence)</td><td>2,340</td><td>468</td><td>468</td><td>3,276</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Zoho Books Professional (about)</td><td>1,265</td><td>1,265</td><td>1,265</td><td class="txt">about 3,795</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Excel route (our fees)</td><td>4,000</td><td>1,500</td><td>1,500</td><td>7,000</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">QuickBooks Online (our fees)</td><td>6,000</td><td>1,500</td><td>1,500</td><td>9,000</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">QuickBooks Desktop (our fees)</td><td>7,000</td><td>1,500</td><td>1,500</td><td>10,000</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Read the table with care. The Wafeq, Tally and Zoho rows include the software itself. The Excel and QuickBooks rows do not. QuickBooks Online plans cost about AED 77 to AED 327 a month on top.</p>
<p>Even so, the pattern is clear. Over three years, built-in software costs a fraction of the outside route. That is why Way 1 comes first.</p>
<p>One caution on Tally. The Silver licence is for one person at a time. If several people use Tally together, you need Gold. Gold costs about AED 7,020 for a new licence and AED 1,404 a year to renew. Ask the question "How many people work in Tally at the same moment?" before you buy.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-5-ask-what-counts-as-one-invoice">
      <h2>Way 5: Ask what counts as one invoice</h2>
<p>Two providers can quote the same price and charge you very different amounts. The reason is how they count.</p>
<p>Ask these questions:</p>
<ul class="know"><li><b>Do credit notes count?</b> In Zoho Books, each credit note you send is one transaction. A sale you correct later can use two or three.</li><li><b>Do received invoices count?</b> Some providers count supplier invoices too. That can double your count. Zoho partner material says received bills may count, so confirm this with Zoho for your account.</li><li><b>Do packs expire?</b> Zoho says unused transactions stay valid while your organisation stays the same. Other providers sell yearly packs that expire.</li><li><b>What happens if I go over?</b> Some charge a higher rate. Some force you to jump to the next pack.</li><li><b>What is free?</b> Zoho gives the first 100 transactions free, <b>once</b>. It is not a yearly gift. Do not assume every provider gives 100 free invoices each year. Many do not.</li></ul>
<p>Here is a real scene. A small trader in Sharjah sends 400 invoices a year. He also receives 400 supplier invoices. Provider A counts only what he sends. His count is 400. Provider B counts both. His count is 800. The same business, the same software, a different bill.</p>
<p>With us, only the sales invoices and credit notes you send are counted. Received invoices are free.</p>
<p>Put the answers in writing. A cheap quote with vague counting rules is not cheap.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-6-keep-your-software-unless-switchin">
      <h2>Way 6: Keep your software unless switching saves real money</h2>
<p>Many owners ask the same thing. "Should I drop QuickBooks and move to Wafeq, Tally or Zoho?"</p>
<p>Maybe. But do the maths on both sides.</p>
<p><b>Reasons to switch:</b></p>
<ul class="know"><li>You want no yearly e-invoicing fee.</li><li>Your QuickBooks Desktop version is old and cannot be connected.</li><li>You planned to change software anyway.</li></ul>
<p><b>Reasons to stay:</b></p>
<ul class="know"><li>You have years of history in your current system.</li><li>Your team knows it well.</li><li>Moving data and retraining staff costs time and money.</li></ul>
<p>The yearly saving can be real. On QuickBooks Online, our fees run AED 1,500 a year at 500 invoices. On Wafeq, e-invoicing adds AED 0. But switching has a one-time cost. We move your data from QuickBooks or Excel and quote the price on WhatsApp, because it depends on your data. Read how <a href="/switch-accounting-software">switching accounting software</a> works before you decide.</p>
<p>A useful rule of thumb: if you keep your software for at least three more years, the saving from switching often wins. If you may change again soon, stay and add an outside ASP.</p>
<p>Using something else, such as Odoo, Sage, Xero, SAP, Oracle or Dynamics? You do not need to switch. These connect to an ASP through a module, an API, a desktop agent or an upload. Each one is priced differently, so we quote by message. See our page for <a href="/other-software">other software</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="way-7-appoint-early-and-test-before-you">
      <h2>Way 7: Appoint early and test before you go live</h2>
<p>Waiting costs money. It costs it in two ways.</p>
<p>First, there are fines. Cabinet Decision No. 106 of 2025 sets them. They are on top of normal VAT penalties.</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="w700"><thead><tr><th>Violation</th><th>Penalty</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="txt">Not appointing an ASP or implementing e-invoicing on time</td><td class="txt">AED 5,000 for each month</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Not issuing or sending an e-invoice</td><td class="txt">AED 100 per invoice, up to AED 5,000 a month</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Not issuing or sending an e-credit note</td><td class="txt">AED 100 per credit note, up to AED 5,000 a month</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Not telling your ASP about business data changes in time</td><td class="txt">AED 1,000 for each day</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Six months late on the appointment alone is AED 30,000. Compare that with a Wafeq plan at AED 690 a year.</p>
<p>Second, there is rush pricing and stress. Data clean-up takes longer than most owners expect. Every business customer needs a correct Tax Registration Number (TRN). Every item needs a VAT code and a standard unit. Fixing this under pressure leads to rejected invoices.</p>
<p>Here are the dates again:</p>
<div class="tablewrap"><table class="w700"><thead><tr><th>Business group</th><th>Appoint your ASP by</th><th>E-invoicing starts</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="txt">Revenue AED 50 million or more</td><td class="txt">30 October 2026 (passed)</td><td class="txt">1 January 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Revenue under AED 50 million</td><td class="txt">31 March 2027</td><td class="txt">1 July 2027</td></tr>
<tr><td class="txt">Government entities</td><td class="txt">31 March 2027</td><td class="txt">1 October 2027</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Your group depends on the gross income in your latest audited financial statements. If you are close to AED 50 million, check that figure first.</p>
<p>Ready early? You can start voluntarily from 1 July 2026. Penalties apply only once your own phase begins.</p>
<p>Before go-live, send one test invoice and one test credit note. A sent e-invoice cannot be edited. You fix a mistake with a credit note, and that is one more document you may pay for.</p>
    </section>

