    <section id="hidden-costs-that-make-a-cheap-quote-exp">
      <h2>Hidden costs that make a cheap quote expensive</h2>
<p>A low headline price is easy to write. These costs are easy to miss.</p>
<ul class="know"><li><b>A higher software plan.</b> Zoho Books needs Professional or higher. The Free and Standard plans do not include e-invoicing. Moving from Standard to Professional adds AED 360 a year on yearly billing.</li><li><b>A lapsed subscription.</b> TallyPrime e-invoicing stops working if TSS lapses. Renew before the date.</li><li><b>Setup and mapping fees.</b> Some providers charge for onboarding, ERP mapping and testing. Ask for the full first-year total in writing.</li><li><b>Data clean-up.</b> Every business customer needs a correct TRN. Every item needs a VAT code. Missing data is a common reason for rejection.</li><li><b>Old software versions.</b> Some older QuickBooks Desktop versions cannot be connected. We check your version first.</li><li><b>A computer that must stay on.</b> With QuickBooks Desktop, invoices go out only while the QuickBooks computer is on and online.</li><li><b>Received documents.</b> Some providers count them. Ask.</li><li><b>Support.</b> Some charge extra for WhatsApp or phone help. Some reply by email only.</li><li><b>Several companies.</b> Each company with its own TRN is set up and appointed separately.</li><li><b>Staff time.</b> Someone must fix rejected invoices and send them again.</li></ul>
<p>Free tools deserve a note. Some standalone portals offer a free tier for very small senders. That can work for a freelancer with a handful of B2B invoices. Read the fine print. Check that the provider is on the Ministry of Finance list. Check that it receives invoices as well as sends them. Check what you pay once you pass the free limit.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="which-cheap-e-invoicing-solution-fits-yo">
      <h2>Which cheap e-invoicing solution fits you?</h2>
<p>Match your situation to a starting point.</p>
<p><b>You send fewer than 10 B2B invoices a month, with no accounting software.</b> Start with the Excel route if you want a managed setup. Or look at a free portal from an accredited provider, after you check its limits. If you plan to grow, consider Wafeq Starter at AED 690 a year.</p>
<p><b>You run a service business with 15 to 400 invoices a month.</b> Zoho Books Professional or Wafeq are the likely winners. Zoho costs about AED 1,265 a year at 500 documents. Wafeq Starter costs AED 690. Pick by the accounting features you need.</p>
<p><b>You are a trader or distributor with many invoices and stock.</b> TallyPrime is the strong fit. There is no per-invoice fee, so high volume stays cheap. Choose Silver for one user or Gold for several.</p>
<p><b>You are a contractor with progress billing, retention and variations.</b> Pick software with approval controls. Zoho Premium and higher add more. Wafeq Plus or Premium may also fit. Read our guide for <a href="/blog/uae-e-invoicing-contractors">contractors</a>.</p>
<p><b>You use QuickBooks and do not want to move.</b> Stay and add an outside ASP. It costs AED 6,000 in year one on QuickBooks Online and AED 7,000 on Desktop, then AED 1,500 a year at 500 invoices. See <a href="/quickbooks-online">QuickBooks Online</a> and <a href="/quickbooks-desktop">QuickBooks Desktop</a>.</p>
<p><b>You use Odoo, Sage, Xero, SAP or another ERP.</b> Message us your software name and invoice count. We send a fixed price, usually the same day.</p>
<p><b>Your revenue is AED 50 million or more.</b> Reliability matters more than the lowest price. Your go-live date is 1 January 2027, and the appointment date has passed. Appoint now.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="a-step-by-step-way-to-choose-a-cheap-e-i">
      <h2>A step-by-step way to choose a cheap e-invoicing solution in Dubai</h2>
<p>Follow these steps in order. They take about an hour.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 1: Confirm you are in scope</h3>
<p>Do you sell to other businesses (B2B) or to government (B2G)? If yes, you are in scope. There is no small-business exemption. Sales to consumers (B2C) are outside the system for now.</p>
<p>A walk-in buyer who gives you a company TRN is a B2B customer. That sale needs an e-invoice once your phase starts. Train counter staff to ask one question: "Is this purchase for a company?"</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 2: Find your deadline</h3>
<p>Under AED 50 million revenue? Appoint by 31 March 2027. Go live on 1 July 2027. AED 50 million or more? Go live on 1 January 2027.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 3: Count your yearly invoices</h3>
<p>Count sales invoices and credit notes you send. Skip supplier invoices and B2C sales. Add a growth margin.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 4: Check if your software is an ASP</h3>
<p>Zoho Books, TallyPrime and Wafeq are. Most other software is not. If yours is not, plan for an outside ASP and a connection.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 5: Price the first three years</h3>
<p>Use the tables in this guide. Add your software plan if it needs a higher tier. Ask each provider for a written first-year total.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 6: Verify accreditation and ask the counting questions</h3>
<p>Check the Ministry of Finance list. Ask what counts as an invoice. Ask about expiry, overage and support.</p>
<h3 class="sm">Step 7: Test, then appoint on EmaraTax</h3>
<p>Log in to EmaraTax, open your business profile and go to the e-invoicing section. Select your ASP, verify with your email and TIN, and submit. Then send a test invoice and a test credit note before your start date.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="do-it-yourself-or-get-help">
      <h2>Do it yourself, or get help?</h2>
<p>On Wafeq, TallyPrime and Zoho Books, you can set up e-invoicing yourself for free. The steps take a few hours if your data is clean. Our guides walk through each one: <a href="/blog/zoho-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Zoho Books</a>, <a href="/blog/tally-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Tally</a> and <a href="/blog/wafeq-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Wafeq</a>.</p>
<p>Get help in three cases. Your data is messy. You have many customers or items. Or you have no time to test.</p>
<p>For those three built-in tools, our setup costs AED 1,500, one time. We check your plan, clean your customer TRNs and VAT codes, handle the EmaraTax appointment, send a test invoice and credit note, and fix rejected invoices.</p>
<p>For QuickBooks, Excel and other software, we handle the whole setup as part of the price. You do not need to do any setup work. Setup takes about 1 week for Excel, 1 to 2 weeks for QuickBooks Online and 2 to 3 weeks for QuickBooks Desktop.</p>
<p>For a deeper look at how our prices are built, read the <a href="/blog/uae-e-invoicing-cost">complete UAE e-invoicing cost guide</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="faq">
      <h2>Cheap e-invoicing solution in Dubai: common questions</h2>
<div class="faq">
<details open><summary>What is the cheapest e-invoicing solution in Dubai?</summary><p>The cheapest route is accounting software that is already an ASP. Wafeq starts at AED 690 a year with no per-invoice fee. TallyPrime has no per-invoice fee with an active TSS of about AED 468 a year. Zoho Books costs about AED 1,265 in year one for 500 documents.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there a free e-invoicing solution in the UAE?</summary><p>The government does not charge you for e-invoicing, but you must use an accredited provider. Some providers offer free tiers for very small senders. Software like TallyPrime and Wafeq includes e-invoicing in the software price. Always check accreditation and the limits of any free plan.</p></details>
<details><summary>How much does e-invoicing cost for a small business in Dubai?</summary><p>It ranges from about AED 690 a year to about AED 7,000 in year one. It depends on your software and invoice count. With us, up to 500 invoices costs AED 6,000 for QuickBooks Online, AED 7,000 for QuickBooks Desktop and AED 4,000 for Excel in year one. Then it is AED 1,500 a year.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Zoho Books cheap for e-invoicing in the UAE?</summary><p>Yes, for most small businesses. You need the Professional plan or higher, which is AED 90 a month on yearly billing. The first 100 transactions are free, once. After that, a pack of 500 costs AED 185 and a pack of 1,000 costs AED 330.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Wafeq e-invoicing free?</summary><p>There is no extra charge and no per-invoice fee. E-invoicing is included in the Starter, Plus and Premium plans. You still pay for the plan: AED 690, AED 960 or AED 2,400 a year.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does TallyPrime charge per e-invoice?</summary><p>No. E-invoicing is included while your TSS subscription is active. TSS Silver renews at about AED 468 a year. TSS Gold renews at about AED 1,404 a year. If TSS lapses, e-invoicing stops working.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I keep using QuickBooks or Excel?</summary><p>Yes. They are not ASPs, so you add an outside ASP. QuickBooks uses a connector. Excel uses an upload template. You do not have to change your accounting software.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do I need e-invoicing if I only sell to consumers?</summary><p>Not for now. Sales to consumers (B2C) are outside UAE e-invoicing. If you also sell to businesses or government, those invoices are in scope.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is a PDF invoice still valid in the UAE?</summary><p>Not for invoices in scope. They must be sent as structured e-invoices in the PINT AE format through an accredited provider. A PDF or scanned invoice does not count. You can still send a PDF as a courtesy copy.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I know if an e-invoicing provider is accredited?</summary><p>Check the Ministry of Finance list of eInvoicing Accredited Service Providers. It shows each provider's legal company name. A provider that is not on the list may be reselling an accredited one. Ask who it is.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the deadline for e-invoicing in the UAE?</summary><p>With revenue under AED 50 million, appoint an ASP by 31 March 2027 and go live on 1 July 2027. With revenue of AED 50 million or more, the appointment date was 30 October 2026 and go-live is 1 January 2027. Government entities go live on 1 October 2027.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the penalty for missing the deadline?</summary><p>Not appointing an ASP on time costs AED 5,000 for each month. After go-live, each invoice not issued electronically can cost AED 100, up to AED 5,000 a month. Credit notes have their own cap.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do supplier invoices I receive count towards the price?</summary><p>With einvoicecost.ae, no. We count only the sales invoices and credit notes you send. Some providers count received documents too, so ask before you sign.</p></details>
<details><summary>Are the prices on this page including VAT?</summary><p>No. All prices exclude 5% VAT. Multiply by 1.05 to get the price including VAT.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I edit an e-invoice after I send it?</summary><p>No. Once sent, an e-invoice cannot be edited or deleted. You correct it with an e-credit note. If the sale must be billed again, you send a new e-invoice.</p></details>
<details><summary>How long does setup take?</summary><p>On Wafeq, TallyPrime or Zoho Books, a few hours to a day if your data is clean. With us, about 1 week for Excel, 1 to 2 weeks for QuickBooks Online and 2 to 3 weeks for QuickBooks Desktop.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can einvoicecost.ae set up my e-invoicing?</summary><p>Yes. For Zoho Books, TallyPrime and Wafeq, setup is AED 1,500, one time. For QuickBooks, Excel and other software, the setup is included in the price you see. Message us your software and invoice count for a fixed quote.</p></details>
</div>
